  {
   "title": "Stressed má- and maká-: by accident",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "To express **unintentional or accidental actions**, attach a **stressed má-** or **maká-** to the beginning of a verb. These verbs show an act happening **beyond the control** of the doer or the receiver."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "Stressed má- and maká-",
     "items": [
      "They have **no imperative** forms.",
      "The accent mark on **má-** and **maká-** is **kept in every tense**.",
      "Not all stressed má- verbs have stressed maká- counterparts."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Verbs using stressed má-"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The forms are made like those of the unstressed ma-. But because the stress stays on **má-** in every tense, the **pronunciation is different**."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Form",
      "Verb",
      "How it is made",
      "Meaning"
     ],
     "rows": [
